{"strongs": "H4294", "word": "מַטֶּה", "translit": "mat.teh", "root": "מטה", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "staff, rod, shaft", "definition": "מַטֶּה 251 noun masculine Exod 4:17 ( feminine Mic 6:9 according to ᵑ0 , but dubious, see below) 1. staff, rod, shaft . 2. branch . 3. tribe ( Eccl 48:2 staff , Eccl 45:6 ; Eccl 45:25 tribe ); — absolute ׳ מ Gen 38:25 +; construct מַטַּה Exod 4:20 +; suffix מַטְּךָ Gen 38:18 + 5 t., מַטֶּ֑ךָ Exod 8:1 , מַטֵּ֫הוּ Isa 10:24 + 10 t.; plural מַטּוֺת 1Kgs 8:1 +, etc.; suffix מַטּוֺחָם Exod 7:12 ; Num 17:21 also מַטָּיו Hab 3:14 (but read מַטֶּיךָ or — Gr — מַטֹּתֶיךָ ); — 1. (compare מַקֵּל , שֵׁבֶט ) staff of traveller Gen 38:18 ; Gen 38:25 ( J ); in general Isa 10:15 (simile; || שֵׁבֶט ); from staff as support comes figurative מַטֵּהלֶֿחֶם staff of bread (food supply) Ezek 4:16 ; Ezek 5:16 ; Ezek 14:13 ; Lev 26:26 ; Ps 105:16 of staff or rod, Moses as shepherd Exod 4:2 ; Exod 4:4 ; Exod 7:15 ( J ), Exod 4:17 ; Exod 7:17 ; Exod 7:20 ; Exod 9:23 ; Exod 10:13 ; Exod 17:5 (all E ); compare also Isa 10:26 ; Exod 14:16 ; Num 20:8 ; Num 20:9 ; Num 20:11 (all P ); called הָאֱלֹהִים ׳ מ Exod 4:20 ; Exod 17:9 (both E ), because of miraculous power connected with it; compare mirac. rod of Aaron Exod 7:9 ; Exod 7:10 ; Exod 7:12 ; Exod 7:19 ; Exod 8:1 ; Exod 8:12 ; Exod 8:13 (all P ), and of Egyptian magicians Exod 7:12 (twice in verse) ( P ); compare Aaron's rod that budded Num 17:18 ; Num 17:21 ; Num 17:23 ; Num 17:25 (compare RS Semitic i. 180; 2d ed. 197 ); carried even by warrior 1Sam 14:27 ; 1Sam 14:43 מַטֵּה שִׁכְמוֺ Isa 9:3 i.e. rod that strikes his shoulder, task-master's rod (|| שֵׁבֶט הַנֹּגֵשׂ בּוֺ ), compare Isa 10:5 and v Isa 10:24 ; Isa 14:5 (|| שֵׁבֶט ), all figurative of oppression; מַטֵּה מוּסָדָה Isa 30:32 appointed rod (of punishment); compare ׳ מ Ezek 7:10 ; Ezek 7:11 (but text obscure, Co — q. v. — sceptre) , also Mic 6:9 according to ᵑ0 , but see below 3 ; used in beating out ( חבט ) fennel Isa 28:27 staff as badge of leader or ruler מַטֵּהעֹֿז Jer 48:17 (|| מַקֵּל ), compare Ps 110:2 so Num 17:17 (4 t. in verse) + 10 t. Num 17 apparently shafts , i.e. arrows or spears, Hab 3:9 ; Hab 3:14 (compare Now Da GASm ). 2. branch of vine Ezek 19:11 ; Ezek 19:12 ; Ezek 19:14 (twice in verse). 3. tribe (183 t.), originally company led by chief with staff: specifically of tribes of Israel in both singular and plural, 1Kgs 7:14 ; 1Kgs 8:1 = 2Chr 5:2 ; Exod 31:2 + 5 t. Exodus; Lev 24:11 ; Num 1:4 + 89 t. Numbers; Josh 7:1 + 56 t. Joshua (all P ); 1Chr 6:45 + 21 t. 1Chr 6 ; 1Chr 12:31 probably also Mic 6:9 (vocative; so ᵐ5 We Now GASm ). — compare שֵׁבֶט , and on relation of these two words for tribe Hebrew usage Dr JPhoenician xi. (1882), 213 f .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5156')\">BDB5156</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H4294')\">H4294</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5155')\">BDB5155</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5157')\">BDB5157</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>מַטֶּה</bdbheb><sub>251</sub> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Exod 4:17\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(2,4,17)\">Exod 4:17</ref></sup> (<b>feminine</b> <ref ref=\"Mic 6:9\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(33,6,9)\">Mic 6:9</ref> according to <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('MT')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ0</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>, but dubious, see below) <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlightword>staff, rod, shaft</highlightword>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> <highlightword>branch</highlightword>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>3.</b> tribe (<checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Eccl 48:2\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(21,48,2)\">Eccl 48:2</ref> <highlight>staff</highlight>, <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Eccl 45:6\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(21,45,6)\">Eccl 45:6</ref>; <chec